   "title": "Gradients of Curves & Areas Under Graphs",
   "content": "<p>To estimate the <strong>gradient of a curve</strong> at a point, draw a <strong>tangent</strong> (a straight line that just touches the curve) and find its gradient.</p><p>To estimate the <strong>area under a curve</strong>, use the <strong>trapezium rule</strong>:</p><p>$$A \\approx \\frac{h}{2}[y_0 + y_n + 2(y_1 + y_2 + \\cdots + y_{n-1})]$$</p><p>where \\(h\\) is the width of each strip.</p>",
   "example": "<p><strong>Estimate area under \\(y = x^2\\) from \\(x = 0\\) to \\(x = 4\\) using 4 strips.</strong></p><p>\\(h = 1\\). \\(y\\)-values: 0, 1, 4, 9, 16.</p><p>\\(A \\approx \\frac{1}{2}[0 + 16 + 2(1 + 4 + 9)] = \\frac{1}{2}[16 + 28] = 22\\)</p>"
  },
